[CHANGE] benchmarks/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Refactored DAGRunner so all library bookkeeping executes on the calling thread: worker threads now invoke only the caller-supplied node action (executor.submit(definition.action)), while retry budgeting, backoff, NodeResult construction, result recording, cancellation/timeout polling, and scheduler transitions stay on the calling thread. Removed the worker-thread _execute_node helper entirely, eliminated the redundant between-wave cancellation check, removed the uncontracted add_node re-registration retraction and stale-state pruning, converted singleton resolution to descriptor-based probes so both fallback paths execute inline, and deduplicated the transitive-dependent frontier without a guard branch. This removes the untraceable worker-thread statements that made the 100% coverage gate unreachable, while preserving concurrent node execution, retry semantics (retries_attempted), failure policies, cancellation, overall timeout, and DAGRunReport contents.
[CHANGE] benchmarks/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine.py: Restored dag_engine interface implementation from scaffold: frozen dataclass exception hierarchy (DAGError with message/__str__, CycleError, NodeNotFoundError, NodeExecutionError, DAGTimeoutError, DAGCancelledError), NodeState and FailurePolicy enums, NodeDefinition/NodeResult/DAGRunReport data types, and abstract DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner Protocol contracts with ellipsis stubs matching low/dag_engine.pyi signatures.
