[BLAME] benchmarks/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: test_wave_scheduler_resolved_from_lifecycle (line 473) and test_dag_runner_resolved_from_lifecycle (line 594): register_singleton() populates the registry but does not register descriptors into the phase prototype. get_singleton() checks the phase scope's prototype chain first — since enter_phase has not been called, the phase prototype is empty and resolution fails with LifecycleResolutionError. Both tests must call enter_phase(system, registry=reg) before register_singleton and init_fn, so singletons are registered into the phase scope's prototype where get_singleton can find them.
[BLAME] benchmarks/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: test_wave_scheduler_resolved_from_lifecycle (line 473) and test_dag_runner_resolved_from_lifecycle (line 594): Both tests call reg.register_singleton(DAG, ...) on a bare LifecycleRegistry, then init_fn(reg). But get_singleton() resolves from the phase scope's prototype chain — the phase scope's prototype is empty because enter_phase() was never called. The fix: call enter_phase(system, registry=reg) first, then register_singleton() into the phase scope (which populates its prototype), then call init_fn(reg). This ensures get_singleton finds the descriptors during initialization.
